<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Remove Floating Meshes</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mesh &gt; Remove &gt; Floating Meshes</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Remove Floating Meshes</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command removes regions of the visible selected object, which are isolated from the main mesh. A mesh entity may contain unconnected areas of triangles. This command will remove these areas that have number of triangles less than the given value. It is possible to remove the whole mesh if you enter a value that exceeds the number of triangles in the largest area. For example, if a mesh consists of two areas with 100,000 and 200 triangles, and you enter 500,000, the whole entity will be deleted.</span></p>
<p><span class="Command">Remove Floating Meshes</span> <span lang="EN-GB">is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. It works on wholly selected entities as well as on partial selections.</span></p>
<p><img src="../mesh/processing_meshes_files/image046.gif" width="257px" height="165px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Remove floating meshes with triangles less than</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Maximum number of connected triangles that must be removed. Default value for this command is 50 triangles.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
