<p><span lang="EN-GB">Sometimes during scanning you may capture areas that are not part of the object but are too close and enter in the range of the laser stripe, for example floor, stand, wall, etc. Also scanning very shiny surfaces may produce reflections that are qualified as surfaces. Later when merge all such false areas will be converted to mesh.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span class="Command">Remove Floating Meshes</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to get rid of such small areas that are not real part of the scanned object.</span></p>
